rcq("R04-B-08-4", "Strengthen / weaken / assumption", "Difficult",
    "Which of the following, if true, would most weaken the claim in paragraph 5 that the governments of independent states must answer for some continuities?",
    "The institutions that seemed to be kept by choice were in fact kept because foreign loans had been made conditional on keeping them.",
    [("Several former imperial powers kept military bases in their former colonies under formal agreements signed with the new governments at the time of independence.",
      "Bases kept by agreement concern the strands former rulers held; nothing here shows that the apparently chosen continuities were not chosen."),
     ("Many members of the new governing elites had been educated in the former metropolis and admired its institutions.",
      "This fits paragraph 3's description of elites 'formed by the old system' who found it 'congenial', so it supports the claim."),
     ("Several newly independent governments wrote entirely new constitutions within a decade of gaining their independence.",
      "This illustrates sovereign power, which paragraph 3 already affirms; it does not bear on whether retained strands were chosen.")],
    "Paragraph 5 says 'If some strands were retained by choice, those governments must answer for the choosing'. The claim rests on the continuities being chosen. Evidence that the apparently chosen ones were in fact kept under financial pressure moves them into the category of strands kept 'by pressure', removing the basis for holding the new governments responsible.",
    "Choosing an option that concerns continuity in general rather than the choice on which responsibility depends.",
    "The solver must identify the conditional on which the claim rests and see which option removes it.",
    cognitive="Analysis", exams=("CAT", "XAT"))

